  {"comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. GitHub #577's design (mitcad#2380; opened with --open, never committed; tools/cli/fillet-dome-pattern-reported-test.cmake): the reporter's build of the public nozzle-on-a-dome benchmark up to its last step. A tube of radii 30 and 40, 60 high, with a hollow hemisphere on it about z (Revolve1 F2; the dome's outer face F2:side(c11[c9,c19]) runs on tangentially into the tube's F2:side(c9[c7,c11])); a nozzle of diameter 40 from a plane 80 from the axis up to the dome (Extrude1 F5, its foot on the dome and the tube), a flange (Extrude2 F7) with eight holes through all (Extrude3 F9, Chamfer1 F10, CircularPattern1 F11), the bore (Extrude4 F13), a groove (Extrude5 F15), Chamfer2 (F16, the bore's edge), Chamfer3 (F17, the flange's outer edge at its underside), Fillet1 (F18, the flange's foot, 2 mm) and Fillet2 (F19, the nozzle's foot, 8 mm)."},
  {"comment": "The benchmark's last step: the nozzle's features, its chamfers and roundings among them, patterned four times about z (CircularPattern2 F20). Before, it failed with 'element 1: there are no bodies in the extrude direction': the copy of the holes through all (F9) was rebuilt against the bodies before the pattern, which end short of the copy's flange."},
  {"cmd": "add_feature", "def": {"type": "circular_pattern",
